Z||000008||Fierobruiser||12-28-2001||08:58 PM||||Yeah, pretty soon John Public will know that GT that's been sitting in his backyard because it wouldn't pass inspection is worth more than a couple of hundred bucks for you to get rid of it. With some national attention it'll have the same status as a GTO or Charger or SS anything. We'll all be lucky to afford one Fiero if at any at all because of the high acquisition price and insurance rates. I'd rather be thought of like a Mini driver, with people wondering what kind of car it is and thinking I'm just a little bit odd. When they ask "didn't they used to burst into flames?" I answer, yes.<P>------------------<BR>Notchbacks Rule<BR>85GT(show car)<BR>88Coupe (daily driver)<BR>84 Coupe(project car)<p>[This message has been edited by Fierobruiser (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||CoolBlue87GT||12-28-2001||09:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierobruiser:<BR><B>With some national attention it'll have the same status as a GTO or Charger or SS anything.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>So let me get this right, are you for this or against it ?<P>||||reg||5
Z||000010||Fierobruiser||12-28-2001||10:02 PM||||I owned sports cars when only 1 percent of people in the US did. I like being different, even unusual. The quickest way for me to loose interest is when something is very popular. Sure it would be nice to own something extremely expensive that few others can own, but I would rather be part of a small group of really interested/ informed people, some who keep their cars perfect while driving them on a regular basis and others who modify the hell out of them to improve the breed. I'm sure you'd like to see your museum piece, "My 87 Fiero GT w/ only 1700 miles was chosen Best of Stock, Best Stock Paint, & Best of Show !!!!!", on TV. I was next to your car at Williamsburg and it's a beautiful display but it's no longer a car. I'm just happy to be able to drive and afford such a great car. The best way to ruin that favorite restaurant that you know about is to tell everybody.<P><P>------------------<BR>Notchbacks Rule<BR>85GT(show car)<BR>88Coupe (daily driver)<BR>84 Coupe(project car)||||reg||1
Z||000011||CoolBlue87GT||12-28-2001||11:56 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierobruiser:<BR><B>I'm sure you'd like to see your museum piece, "My 87 Fiero GT w/ only 1700 miles was chosen Best of Stock, Best Stock Paint, & Best of Show !!!!!", on TV.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, I'd like them to come to a show like Daytona, or Carlisle and get all the different models and interview <B>all the owners.</B><P>My intent to contact them was not about me or my car.  It was to have a show produced about the history of the Fiero, and the people the how we all enjoy them in different forms.<P>The history is really something that should be documented. <P>So to all, get this, it's not about me or my car. <B>IT'S FOR ALL THE FIEROS'S.</B><P><p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 12-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||CoolBlue87GT||12-29-2001||09:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierobruiser:<BR><B> I was next to your car at Williamsburg and it's a beautiful display but it's no longer a car.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, I remember, You have that nice black notchback.<P>Uh hmmm, Well I guess since it's no longer a car, gee, guess I'll throw it out.<P>What a statement. Just because a car's not driven much, SO WHAT.<P>Blackstang went round & round on this with me.<P>If someone chooses to put a V8 in their car, good for them. If someone changes their car into a convertable, good for them<P>That's a choice they made, & I think it's great.<P>Now, if someone want's to keep their car under wraps and doesn't drive it much - SO WHAT, it does not make it "not a car any more"<P>A huge reason my car has not been driven is because of the work schedule I kept during the 1st 11 years of owning the car.<P>Working around the clock 7 days a week, many 20 hour days, simply exuasted me and gave me no time to enjoy the car by driving it.<P>That was a choice I made, It made me lots of money, but I lost alot of "life" by doing so.<P>I will let no one ridicule the choice I made, key words here are, "the choice I made"<P>When someone goes off on me for having a Fiero that's "a museum piece" , or saying "it's no longer a car"<P>Well to me I take those statments as if their saying,  boy that guys a jerk for not driving that car.<P>To that I say, wait, it goes deeper than just not driving it for the reasons I detailed above. It was and is my choice to own this car and to keep it the way I see fit.<P>I'm not starting a flame war, just don't enjoy anyone telling me I've done something wrong.||||reg||9
Z||000013||LoW_KeY||12-29-2001||09:33 AM||||I did that and they said they would take it into consideration.. they had the history of pontiac and guess what they skipped the fiero.. <P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/low_keysig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Master_Sushi||12-29-2001||12:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by CoolBlue87GT:<BR><B> It was and is my choice to own this car and to keep it the way I see fit.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I respect you allot for that! I wouldn't be able to keep myself from driving a mint gt if I had one. Its people like you that will allow others in the future to see what a new fiero looks like.||||reg||1
